      "type": "text",
      "text": "Children 1 to 5 y: chronic submaxillary/submandibular cervical lymphadenitis is commonly due to MAC or M. scrofulaceum. Excision is USU adequate tx; antibiotics (eg, macrolides) may be needed for recurrent or recalcitrant cases."
